  #define FMC_BTR3_DATAST_POS       INT32_C(8)    /** @brief Data-phase duration these bits are written by software to define the duration of the data phase (refer to figure81 to figure93), used in asynchronous accesses: for each memory type and access mode data-phase duration, please refer to the respective figure (figure81 to figure93). Example: mode1, write access, DATAST=1: data-phase duration= DATAST+1 = 2 KCK_FMC clock cycles. Note: in synchronous accesses, this value is dont care.. */
